  "implemented_behavior": "Weighted trusted concept facets and relation fidelity without keyword-overlap grading.",
  "bounded_contract": "Reference concepts have id,positive weight,nonempty typed facets; reference relations have id,weight,from,predicate,to. Candidate concepts omit weight; relations omit weight.\nA concept earns matched required facets/number required facets times its weight. Missing/wrong facets lose credit. Unexpected facets are defects even if required facet recall is complete. Missing concepts stay in denominator; unknown IDs and duplicates rejected.\nEach relation is all-or-zero: exact directed triple and both endpoints actually supplied/taught. Reference concept/relation unit-ID collisions rejected. Input list order does not change unit scoring.",
  "bounds_and_open_scope": "No free-text paraphrase understanding, arbitrary semantic equivalence, learner comprehension or human-rater agreement measured. Trusted graph annotation quality needs independent review.",
